    <td align="left" vAlign="top" bgcolor=#000000>&nbsp;
		<table align="left" border="0" cellPadding="1" cellSpacing="1" width="100%" bgcolor=#000000>
        
			<tr>
				<td style="WIDTH: 15px" width="15"></td>
				<td align="left" class="TextMain" bgcolor=#000000>
					<center><h2> Guild Rules And Conduct</h2></center>
		        <P>
					The following rules have been established to make our playing time more enjoyable and not as a means to take away from an individual’s total gaming experience.
					<br><br>
					1) Conduct and Character Issues:
					<br><br>
					With regard to conduct and attitudes, we encourage people to have fun, laugh and enjoy each other’s company. Do not participate in offensive behavior that may be degrading to other members or even yourself. Please try to police your own actions or they may be reviewed for guild disciplinary actions by our officers.
					<br><br>
					Some of the more serious offenses are kill stealing, deliberate deception and any attempt to defraud guild members as well as other players. Our guild members should adhere to the General Guidelines as indicated by Verant. Lying, undermining other members, begging or leaving your wiped out group without offering to help are examples of conduct we wish not have associated with At Deaths Door. When in doubt about a conduct issue, contact a guild officer for advice - "Ignorance" is not a viable excuse.
					<br><br>
					Its every guild members duty to act as a guild custodian and police not only your own, but others actions of guild members. Please be discreet when handling these situations and not openly berate members in an open guild chat forum unless no other recourse is available.
					<br><br>
					Use common sense when dealing with problems with guildmates and others. Try to solve any problems that you may encounter on your own at first. If you cannot, then please get an officer involved before making snap decisions. Disbanding from the guild “in the heat of the moment” is frowned upon and likely you will not get a re-invite. Disbanding from the guild will result in the loss of all GPK points.
					<br><br>
					At Death’s Door does not condone a player having characters in a variety of guilds and require that all characters are associated with this guild. 
					<br><br>
					2) Guild Chat:
					<br><br>
					This guild has open enrollment to many diverse age groups, so we as guild members have an obligation to keep chat relatively free of offensive language and any connotations toward sexual or racial content. Please respect each other and use discretion as appropriate. We strive to be as helpful as possible with quests, advice, pricing and other game topics. Guild Chat should be a non-discriminatory harassment free environment.
					<br><br>
					3) Interaction:
					<br><br>
					Guild members should strive to be as helpful as possible as time merits. The reputation of all us as individuals will have a big impact of how others view us as a guild. Be courteous and friendly to other players on the server.
					<br><br>
					4) Power Leveling:
					<br><br>
					If you do “power level” then we ask you to use discretion and keep it out of guild chat. Players should “never” expect help from the guild with power leveling or twinking.
					<br><br>
					5) Guild Based items and Skills:
					<br><br>
					We request (not require) that guild members with trade skills offer their assistance to guildmates at close to cost with regards to any items which need to be purchased to make a particular item.
					<br><br>
					If an item is given to you by another guildmate, and you don’t require its use anymore, then we ask that you pass it on to another guildmate of appropriate level when appropriate.
					<br><br>
					6) Guild Invites :
					<br><br>
					a) Currently, the minimum level for guild invite is of the 50th season unless otherwise authorized by the guild leader. It is the responsibility of our officers to strictly adhere and enforce this rule. All persons joining At Death’s Door must fill out an application in order to start earning GPKs with the guild. 
					<br><br>
					b) All new invites will go through a 6 week trial period to assess that persons conduct and playing habits. They will be known as “Recruits” during this stage. While in this trial period, the 'Recruit' is still subject to ADD rules regarding dismissals (see following section on guild dismissals). We do allow recruits to earn GPKs with the guild so a completed application is essential.
					<br><br>
					c) All new invites are the ultimate responsibility of the person who invited them during their initial trial stage. After the trial stage, any disciplinary action, which may need to take place, will be subject to ADD dismissal policy.
					<br><br>
					d) Upon initial guild invite, the inviting officer must first make the new invite aware of the ADD rule section on our website. The inviting officer must notify a recruitment officer about the player invite. 
					<br><br>
					e) During the first six week period, the Recruit will not receive any help for quest items. After this time, they will receive the full support of the guild on their quests. Recruits should be present at a majority of our scheduled raids during their six week trial. 
					<br><br>
					7) Dismissals:
					<br><br>
					a) Once a month a panel of officers meet to discuss any breaches of guild or game protocol.
					<br><br>
					b) Offenses to guild protocol will be handled in such a manner that the offending player will receive two verbal warnings from any officer via private tells before additional disciplinary action is taken.
					<br><br>
					c) It is not the responsibility of any one officer to dismiss a player without that player having their proverbial day in court (see line D). A dismissal ruling can bypassed if an offense is serious enough that the player is causing a great disruption to the guild. 
					<br><br>
					d) A dismissed player can petition the guild leader for re-admittance. Upon re-admittance the offending person should provide a guild apology in guild chat for his actions. 
					<br><br>
					e) Dismissals are handled in such a manner only when all avenues of action are exhausted. Guild dismissal is not an arbitrary action but one that should be taken into great consideration. We as guild members have an obligation to educate our fellow guildmates on conduct becoming of an ADD member. Unless all avenues of discipline have been exhausted or the offense is of an extremely serious nature, then dismissal is warranted only by consensus of “3” guild officers. The dismissing officer upon taking this course of action must notify the player of his offense and what course of action he can take to get re-admitted to the guild. 
					<br><br>
					f) After dismissal, any player may then petition the guild leader for re-admittance to the guild. The guild leader must poll the officers and a ruling will be considered. 
				</P>
